From a0b6bd8152ae9584381dd43e9d27c0619c141cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:22:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(bore): pin the centre-cutting law on the milled Bore's
 way in

The Bore ride rides the planar ladder, whose every descent asks the
centre-cutting law (M11.3, 874507a8 / 515525c4): a cutter that is not
centre-cutting ramps into an undrilled hole along the radial sweep, or
the op is refused by name where no ramp or helix fits; it never plunges
into solid. Three app tests pin it, and the centre-cutting cutter's
axial plunge as the audit's control.

Refs #1036

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
